From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: cold hints only while the host is short of RAM; on the PS5 that is never, so the upload notes, page walks and region scans stop (zortos293/Lichii #1581 e633e165f7), off by default

Switch: EDEN_UP_COLD_HINT_GATE=1 (exact "1", read once, at the first upload or cold hint). Off, or
any other value: exactly T151. On, the first use logs "EDEN_UP_COLD_HINT_GATE: cold hints only
while the host is short of RAM (available-memory figure on this host: none, so never)" (LOG_INFO,
Common_Memory). On the PS5 it should say "none, so never".

What: the texture and buffer caches note every upload of 64 KiB / 256 KiB and more. Every 600
frames, on the GPU thread, TextureCache::TickFrame and BufferCache::TickFrame hand each noted range
to DeviceMemoryManager::HintCold, which walks the range page by page, builds a list of runs, makes
the "DeviceMemory:ColdHint" worker thread on first use and queues the runs to it. Every 30 s the
nx2:ColdHint thread takes the gsv region lock and builds a list of every block of every GPU-only
region (the game's texture pools, GBs), then hints each one. At the end of all that,
HostMemory::HintCold does nothing on the PS5: its body is VirtualUnlock on Windows, MADV_PAGEOUT on
Linux, and nothing else (host_memory.cpp, checked). So on our console all of it is work for nothing,
some of it on the GPU thread and under a lock guest map calls also take, plus short allocations at
the moments memory is lowest.

Upstream (#1581) makes both HintCold paths return unless less than a quarter of the RAM, and less
than 4 GiB, is available (Common::GetAvailablePhysicalMemory, read at most once a second). Its
available-memory read has a body only for Windows and Linux; elsewhere it returns 0, which counts
as "not short", so on a host like ours upstream never hints. This patch takes that code as is
(memory_detect.h/.cpp, the two early returns) behind the switch, and adds one thing of ours:
with the switch on, on a host whose HintCold does nothing, the two caches no longer note uploads
at all (Common::ColdHintRecord), so the range lists and the sparse-segment walk at upload stop too.
On Windows and Linux the notes are kept and only the hint is gated, as upstream.

Why a switch and not unconditional: it changes nothing a player can see on the PS5 (the hint is a
no-op here), but it removes a thread and moves work and allocations, so it gets its own A/B like
any memory change. Off cost: one cached bool test per HintCold call (every 600 frames per range,
every 30 s per region pass) and one non-inline call returning a cached bool per noted upload.

Test: memory census (EDEN_UP_MEM_CENSUS=1) at the big loads, on against off: lowest free memory
not lower, no new hitch at the 600-frame ticks (frame times every 20 s at 30 fps). The start log
must have the line above. A thread list (if a probe gives one) should lack DeviceMemory:ColdHint.
Do not expect an fps change; the walk is small. What it can show: fewer short allocations at a load.

Not taken from upstream: its unit test (our core has no src/tests).

Origin and credit: zortos293 (Zortos), zortos293/Lichii PR #1581, commit e633e165f7 (13 Nov 2026),
ported there from ThatGuyMcd/Lichii-TGM c3fa9cb010 by Julius Bairaktaris (cherry-pick of
eb19f75dfb; idea from Fritchii EXP8 by Frizti), compared there with Eglantine nx2-experimental
3b87091034 / 42fdfac891 by kraibse (PR #825). The record-side skip is ours.
---
diff --git a/src/common/memory_detect.cpp b/src/common/memory_detect.cpp
index 86a3abc..5fc41cb 100644
--- a/src/common/memory_detect.cpp
+++ b/src/common/memory_detect.cpp
@@ -12,11 +12,19 @@
 #include <sys/sysctl.h>
 #elif defined(__linux__)
 #include <sys/sysinfo.h>
+#include <sys/mman.h>
 #else
 #include <unistd.h>
 #endif
 #endif
 
+#include <atomic>
+#include <chrono>
+#include <cstdio>
+#include <cstdlib>
+#include <cstring>
+
+#include "common/logging.h"
 #include "common/memory_detect.h"
 
 namespace Common {
@@ -69,4 +77,75 @@ const MemoryInfo& GetMemInfo() {
     return mem_info;
 }
 
+// EDEN_UP_COLD_HINT_GATE (0755): zortos293/Lichii #1581 (e633e165f7, ported there from
+// ThatGuyMcd/Lichii-TGM c3fa9cb010 by Julius Bairaktaris; idea from Fritchii EXP8 by Frizti).
+u64 GetAvailablePhysicalMemory() {
+#ifdef _WIN32
+    MEMORYSTATUSEX memorystatus;
+    memorystatus.dwLength = sizeof(memorystatus);
+    if (!GlobalMemoryStatusEx(&memorystatus)) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    return memorystatus.ullAvailPhys;
+#elif defined(__linux__)
+    // MemAvailable counts the page cache the kernel can drop, which sysinfo's freeram doesn't.
+    std::FILE* const file = std::fopen("/proc/meminfo", "r");
+    if (file == nullptr) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    u64 available_kib = 0;
+    char line[128];
+    while (std::fgets(line, sizeof(line), file) != nullptr) {
+        unsigned long long value = 0;
+        if (std::sscanf(line, "MemAvailable: %llu kB", &value) == 1) {
+            available_kib = value;
+            break;
+        }
+    }
+    std::fclose(file);
+    return available_kib * 1024;
+#else
+    return 0;
+#endif
+}
+
+bool IsHostLowOnMemory() {
+    using Clock = std::chrono::steady_clock;
+    static std::atomic<Clock::rep> checked_at{};
+    static std::atomic<bool> low{};
+    const Clock::rep now = Clock::now().time_since_epoch().count();
+    const Clock::rep last = checked_at.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
+    if (last == 0 || now - last >= Clock::duration{std::chrono::seconds{1}}.count()) {
+        checked_at.store(now, std::memory_order_relaxed);
+        low.store(IsLowOnMemory(GetAvailablePhysicalMemory(), GetMemInfo().TotalPhysicalMemory),
+                  std::memory_order_relaxed);
+    }
+    return low.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
+}
+
+bool ColdHintGate() {
+    static const bool enabled = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_COLD_HINT_GATE");
+        const bool on = value != nullptr && std::strcmp(value, "1") == 0;
+        if (on) {
+            LOG_INFO(Common_Memory,
+                     "EDEN_UP_COLD_HINT_GATE: cold hints only while the host is short of RAM "
+                     "(available-memory figure on this host: {})",
+                     GetAvailablePhysicalMemory() != 0 ? "yes" : "none, so never");
+        }
+        return on;
+    }();
+    return enabled;
+}
+
+bool ColdHintRecord() {
+    // Same platform test as HostMemory::HintCold (host_memory.cpp): keep the two in step.
+#if defined(_WIN32) || (defined(__linux__) && defined(MADV_PAGEOUT))
+    return true;
+#else
+    static const bool record = !ColdHintGate();
+    return record;
+#endif
+}
+
 } // namespace Common
